<title>HONG KONG: Union Bank of Taiwan mandates US$50 mln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Union Bank of Taiwan mandates US$50 mln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Taiwan has mandated three banks to arrange a US$50 million floating rate certificate of deposit issue, bankers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The facility has a final maturity of three years with a put option in year two.</p>
<p>Price talk is around 32 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate, they said. Syndication will start next week.</p>
<p>The deal has been fully underwritten.</p>
<p>Arrangers are WestLB, Societe Generale Asia and First Chicago Bank.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
